    "body": "**TLDR:** `examples/verifiers/generation_server.py` moves to `generator/generation_server.py` with no content change, and its imports follow. PR 9 serves it from each generator.\n\n**Stack** (14 PRs, merge bottom-up; this PR is in **bold**)\n\n| # | PR | Independent? | Needs (stack positions) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Verifiers 0.4.0 | yes | — |\n| 2 | Verifiers: release each finished rollout's routing session | yes | — (resolves its test overlap with 1) |\n| 3 | Verifiers generation server: no per-request access log | yes | — |\n| 4 | Verifiers generation server: faster request path, required sampling params | yes | — (resolves its test overlap with 1-3) |\n| 5 | Rollout workers write structured logs | yes | — |\n| 6 | Drain in-flight rollouts during shutdown | yes | — |\n| 7 | Generator drains itself before a hot_swap=False weight load | yes | — |\n| **8** | **Move GenerationServer to torchtitan/rl/generator** | **yes, in code** | **— (moves the file 3 and 4 edit)** |\n| 9 | Every generate call goes over HTTP to its generator | no | 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8 |\n| 10 | Generator aborts a request whose caller left | no | 9 |\n| 11 | Cancel a rollout group on its worker | no | 5, 6, 9 |\n| 12 | Run Verifiers groups in rollout workers | no | 9, 11 |\n| 13 | Optional native rollout timeout | no | 12 |\n| 14 | Rollouts that fail outside the policy are recorded, not trained | no | 12, 13 |\n\n```text\ntorchtitan/rl/{examples/verifiers => generator}/generation_server.py   (rename, no content change)\nimports updated: examples/verifiers/rollouter.py, examples/verifiers/README.md,\n                 torchtitan_recipes/rl/verifiers_dapo_math.py, verifiers_terminal_bench.py,\n                 tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_verifiers.py\n```\n\nYou may ask: why its own PR? Combined with PR 9's edits, the move is only 54% similar, just above git's 50% rename cutoff, so a later edit can turn it into a delete plus a new file. On its own it's a 100% rename, reviewed at a glance.\n\n**Test plan**\n```bash\npytest tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu   # verifiers 0.4.0: 552 passed, 3 skipped (same as PR 7)\n```\n",
